WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:07.940
You touched my hand when I stretched them out so far...

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.750
Just one word is fine.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.580
Just voice your dreams.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:28.710
It's your first step and first sign to realization.

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:32.800
Ask yourself what is it that you like?

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:34.930
Your answers will...

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:39.930
blow your questions high into the sky.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:36.340
Even more...

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:38.220
Like fireworks...

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:46.440
Even though we should all try to be more honest we ourselves, we can't.

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:53.440
Maybe I should try summoning my soul as a child?

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:59.990
What touched my hand when i stretched them out so far...

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:05.120
was a Supernova that suddenly appear to this new night.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:11.090
For millions of light years, it never stops inside of me.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:19.300
The longer I gaze, the more power my eyes absorb...

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:24.560
and that's because... because I'm a star too!

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:31.020
Escaping the pursuit of Mihoshi,

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:31.020
Saku finds himself in the library.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:36.030
There, Saku has a chance encounter

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:36.030
with the Student President, Kotozuka Fumie.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:39.530
It's been almost two months since the Entrance Ceremony.

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:42.910
Freshmen are changing into their summer uniforms for the first time.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:46.160
Yoko, you look cute in it.

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.170
I bought it with my first paycheck.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:52.000
The freshmen learn to dress sloppy.

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:55.590
I hope people don't think I'm trying to look cute even though I'm tall.

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:56.420
Don't worry.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:59.510
Boys that stand out start to appear.

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:02.180
Even coed groups start to form.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:10.190
And this is also the time when idols who didn't stand out at first, surprise us and start to appear.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.400
Say, is that Nishimoto-kun?

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:14.570
He's really cool.

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:18.320
There is one man who's trying to hide in his shadow and to move to a place where he doesn't stand out.

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:17.070
Why didn't he cut his hair until now?

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:19.200
You're right!

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:21.120
Good job, Nishimoto.

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:22.950
I've been waiting for something like this.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.080
Please continue to be the center of attention!

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:27.000
Hey, Ooyagi!

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:30.460
What's with you? You look sleepy. It's still morning.

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:33.710
Edogawa, I'm trying not to stand out right now.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:36.010
Morning!

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:37.590
The headliner's here!

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:40.470
Last night was amazing.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.050
Did you have a hard time this morning after such a late night?

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:47.390
I was so excited that I couldn't sleep when I got home.

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:51.400
How should I say this... It was like I was itching inside.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:54.940
Those nights must be what people call an "exciting night."

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:56.030
"Exciting"?!

00:02:58.150 --> 00:02:58.860
Go back!

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:00.820
Go back to your own classroom!

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:04.990
What's wrong with you, Saku-chan?

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:10.250
It's me, dear. Open up!

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:12.170
Everything's wrong! I'm always telling you to stop coming to my class and hugging me!

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:12.580
What's wrong, dear?!

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:14.420
Huh?

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:19.380
Mihoshi?

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:23.260
I won't let you rest tonight either.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:25.510
Noooo!

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:27.600
Older girlfriends are amazing!

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:28.270
You're misunderstanding!

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:30.440
Hey, tell me more!

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:32.850
Ooyagi-kun <i>is </i> making progress.

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:37.230
Stargazing Session~!

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:36.520
Don't say stuff that can be misunderstood and then just disappear!

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:43.570
Why does Mihoshi always cause a mess?

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:46.660
That's just her way of saying "Hi."

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:49.950
You were just dragged into doing some stargazing with her yesterday, right?

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:54.330
I think the last stargazing session when we went with everyone must have put her in a good mood.

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:56.500
She's been dragging me there almost every night lately.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:01.090
She dragged me to do stargazing and moon gazing because the moon was setting at midnight.

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:03.340
Lucky you! Rather, let me join!

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:07.720
Although I also thought the last stargazing session went well...

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:11.730
But books that I want to read are starting to pile up, and I can't get any sleep either.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:15.810
And earlier, it was the perfect opportunity not to stand out...

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.190
Hm... I doubt it.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:22.070
Anyways, what I want is a quiet high school life.

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:24.990
My body won't be able to handle any more attention.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:27.990
Everyone's probably just enjoying the rumors.

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:30.620
Most people won't take them seriously.

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:32.080
I sure hope so.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:33.710
It'll be fine.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:35.790
It'll be the weekend starting tomorrow.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.590
Just sleep well. It'll blow away your worries.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:40.550
O-Ooyagi-kun...

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:40.960
Hm?

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:52.140
I-Is it true that you did <i>this</i> and <i>that</i> with Mihoshi-senpai last night?

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:55.100
She's taking this seriously! And the rumor is getting exaggerated!

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:57.100
No, absolutely not!

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.440
But... everyone says that...

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:00.020
"Everyone"?

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:02.860
Please...

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:06.450
Please stop this!

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:11.410
Saku-chan, look, it's the stars.

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:13.580
You're right. They're amazing...

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:18.290
You always just read books, so I'll show you a lot of them.

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:21.460
Wait. Mii-chan!

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:23.260
Mii-chan!

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:30.430
Ew, you only play with girls!

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:31.640
What beautiful stars.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:33.520
Even though he just transferred-

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:35.230
Look, it's the boy from the rumors.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:37.520
He just transferred here too...

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:38.860
So your name is Saku-kun?

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:39.310
Attention.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:41.360
Bow.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:42.020
Huh?

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:43.860
Oh.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:47.450
I'm at my limit.

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.620
What? Saku-chan left?

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:52.410
Er... yeah...

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:55.370
When I turned around after class ended, he was already gone.

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:57.790
And I found this message on his desk.

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:00.880
This is all your fault.

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:02.380
Why?

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:07.340
I had an amazing plan for tonight too!

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:07.300
Mihoshi...

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:13.720
I should have done this earlier.

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:16.980
There's no reason why I have to let her drag me around all the time.

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:19.520
I wonder why I didn't realize this earlier?

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:23.480
Saku-chan, wait!

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:27.240
I'm not going to worry about it and I'll spend the rest of the day the way I want.

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:33.620
Oh, the smell of paper.

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:38.870
Look, it's the Japanese story collection published by Keidansha.

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:43.040
Books: Complete Japanese Literature Collection

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:41.880
I used to read them a lot in the other places I lived.

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:52.140
You're... Akeno's boyfriend!

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:54.180
I'm not...

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:55.890
Here you go.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:57.980
Oh, thank you.

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:00.390
I'll pay.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:02.310
It's okay.

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:04.270
It's my apology for interrupting your research.

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:07.150
No, I don't want Akeno's boyfriend treating me.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:08.780
Like I said, I'm not Akeno's boyfriend.

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:10.740
We're just childhood friends, no... She's a predator!

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:11.410
Er...

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:13.660
Let's stop arguing...

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:14.950
You're right.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:17.790
Then what are you doing here by yourself?

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:18.700
What happened to the club?

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:21.250
I... took some time off.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:25.000
The Astronomy Club's activities themselves are like time-outs from life.

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:28.800
Besides, there's no way a club run by Akeno could be normal.

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:32.090
No, it might not look like it, but we <i>are </i>active.

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:37.930
Although that's not something someone who ran away should be saying.

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:43.520
I have no intention of arguing with you, an Astronomy Club member,

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.070
but didn't the idea of joining the Literature Club cross your mind?

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:49.940
You like books, don't you?

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:54.740
Even if you joined that club just because Akeno asked you to,

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:57.330
I don't think you have to feel obligated to stay.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:07:58.660
That's not-

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:00.790
She's right.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:03.920
An obligation from having misunderstood her for seven years...

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:07.420
I love books.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:11.550
I love stories, books themselves, and the atmosphere they bring.

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:14.340
I was also interested in the Literature Club.

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:19.350
But as I take a good look up at the sky after all these years,

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:22.440
a part of me is awed too.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:24.940
Is that so.

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:32.400
The Literature Club lacks male members so you would be a big asset if you joined...

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:33.030
Huh?

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:37.280
Keep at it until the club's disbanded.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:40.040
So you still hate us.

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:41.250
Of course.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:46.750
No matter what city I moved to,
I felt comfortable as long as I had books.

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:53.090
It was because regardless of what city I was in,
if I flipped a page, the same scenes appeared.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:09:00.390
Sometimes when I see someone reading a book I like, it makes me happy and want to talk to them.

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:05.560
But I could never actually talk to them.

00:09:06.310 --> 00:09:08.400
It's because I'm always worried about what others think of me.

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:14.240
Oh how wonderful it would be if I could actually bring myself to talk to them.

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:17.990
Later on, I regret it a little.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:25.580
That's right. Mii-chan just wants to share her experiences too.

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:29.750
And she is honest with her feelings.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:34.590
Right now, and in the past too.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:38.800
Huh?

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:41.970
Ah... Saku-chan.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:45.730
Mii-chan.

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:47.850
I'm... sorry.

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:49.190
Huh?

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:54.780
Sayo-chin scolded me.

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:57.610
It seems like I've overdone it again.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:00.990
But I was so happy that I could be with you again.

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:04.910
I was so happy that I could stargaze with you again...

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:07.330
So I couldn't help myself...

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:09.920
I'm really sorry!

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:15.590
It's okay. I understand.

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:17.760
I'm sorry too.

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:20.640
I'm just worried about what others think of me.

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:22.970
I should have told you.

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:26.350
If you don't force me, I'll join you again

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:28.390
on your stargazing.

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:33.900
Okay! Okay! Okay!

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:36.150
Then let's go tonight!

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:36.440
What?

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:38.570
Look, the moon and the planets are-

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:40.820
Hey, you didn't understand a thing!

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:44.410
Ah!

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:49.460
Onee-chan, that's my hair dryer!

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:51.880
Oh, Hime, good morning.

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:54.380
Come on, let me use it.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:56.630
I left you mine in exchange, didn't I?

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:59.380
This is horrible. It's too stiff!

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:02.600
Your hair's straight so you don't need to use it at all!

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:04.760
You're so annoying.

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:13.020
Hm, I think it's... dwarf level 2... no about dwarf level 3.

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:15.980
It's going to rain soon. Maybe I'll bundle it.

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:16.530
Huh?

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:20.990
My hair isn't for measuring humidity!

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:24.660
Tsuyu.

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:32.120
A rainy season between June and mid-July observed in East-Asian countries like Japan and China.

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:39.170
My book is wet again.

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:41.510
I shouldn't have brought it with me.

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:45.220
Even though we put tissues in between and pressed it shut.

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:47.430
Thanks for all your ideas.

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:51.230
I wonder why I am sad when paper gets wet.

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:53.480
It makes it sticky.

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:58.570
But it's only after a blessed rain that I give up on reading books on the street.

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:00.860
So books interest you until they get wet?

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:04.070
But it sure has been raining a lot lately.

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:07.660
I doubt we can do much today either.

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:09.620
What happened to your Photography Club?

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:11.330
I've been attending it. Don't worry.

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:13.420
Hello!

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:14.750
Hm?

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:25.260
Hey!

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:26.720
What's wrong? What happened?

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:29.390
I'm sorry, I stepped on you! I stepped on you!

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:29.390
Get a hold of yourself, Mii-chan!

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:31.180
My foot did it! My foot did it!

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:30.600
What happened? Get a hold of yourself!

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:31.930
Mihoshi.

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:33.980
I... can't see the stars...

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:36.440
For... days....

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:41.030
Oh no!

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:42.150
Edogawa, get the futon ready!

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:42.700
Roger!

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:45.570
S-Stars...

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:46.910
Huh?

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:51.410
Geez, she surprised me.

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:54.210
It's an annual thing.

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:58.590
It's like her switch turns off when she can't see the stars for a long period of time.

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:02.380
When she was little, she was like this in classes too.

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:03.590
Ah.

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:07.970
Because of that, I was always her watchdog in the classroom.

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:12.560
You're the one who's amazing, Sayo-senpai.

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:15.730
But it's not like it rains everyday.

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:17.100
She's just overreacting.

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:17.900
Yes...

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:20.520
That's why it gets my hopes up.

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:24.780
It looks like the weather's nice until night actually falls.

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:27.570
But as the sun sets...

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:29.370
Ah, a cloud is forming.

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:31.040
Huh? What?

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:34.330
And it repeats over and over!

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:36.460
I understand now, so calm down.

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:38.460
Shut up, Astronomy Club!

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:40.000
Fumin!

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:45.760
What a useless club, incapable of being active when it rains.

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:52.260
As a side note, the Literature Club is active no matter the weather.

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:54.770
Yes, I know that.

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:58.900
Oh, if you do, then stop making me repeat myself.

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:03.440
Fine.

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:08.700
I'll show you just how active the Astronomy Club is!

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:09.370
Hm?

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:14.160
Therefore, here we go Saku-chan, Hime-chan!

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:16.830
If you're going to stargaze, you'll need some knowledge too.

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:21.000
Astronomy Club Quiz Show!

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:26.340
Even amaze NASA with the knowledge you'll acquire as you answer the questions.

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:29.760
First, look at the picture and say the constellation's name.

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:32.430
Question number one.

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:38.100
I know! Cassiopeia!

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:45.030
Do you have the dedication to really do this?

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:49.820
I thought so. A useless club will always be useless.

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:52.280
Maybe disbanding would be the best for you guys.

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:55.870
I know!

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:56.450
Huh?

00:14:57.790 --> 00:14:59.500
Wow, amazing!

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:03.090
It's the first time I've visited a museum or a planetarium!

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:04.800
Look, it's a head cut-out.

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:06.210
Say, take a picture of me.

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:06.840
Hurry!

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:08.220
Orb!

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:14.560
The sun's huge!

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:16.520
That's the spirit, Edogawa-kun!

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:19.270
The crow that was crying earlier is smiling already.

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:18.230
Jupiter's huge too!

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:20.060
That's right, Edogawa-kun.

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:23.980
But you are indeed smart-to decide to come to the planetarium so suddenly.

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:22.230
Pluto's tiny!

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:24.060
That's right, Edogawa-kun!

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:27.940
I thought I'd appeal to her activities.

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:29.700
She saw me take a break from the club so...

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:33.120
Have you been here before?

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:34.950
Yes, I have. Once.

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:37.080
Although it was a long time ago.

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:40.160
Mihoshi's father brought Mihoshi and I here.

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:42.290
Mihoshi-chan! Sayo-chan!

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:44.290
Haruko-san!

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:46.750
Has it been two months since you last came here?

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:51.380
Hello. I'm Hatori Haruko, a navigator.

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:55.220
Good day, mademoiselle.

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:56.350
I-

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:57.010
Cut it out.

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:01.060
I see, so everyone's in the same club.

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:02.020
I envy you.

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:04.940
It wasn't until college that I made a group of friends.

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:08.860
You were this small when we first met.

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:12.110
Time sure flies.

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:13.660
But I'm happy.

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:18.040
I want more people to come during seasons like this when stars are more "distant."

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:20.160
Of course, please come during the other seasons too.

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:23.420
Yes, I'll come a lot. Even every day!

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:26.290
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:29.840
I had the air conditioning turned down because we haven't had many visitors.

00:16:30.050 --> 00:16:30.260
Huh?

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:32.300
U-Um...

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:34.300
A bad hair day is a woman's worry. I understand you.

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:35.760
Use this.

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:36.180
Huh?

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:41.310
Um...

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:42.940
Now, come this way.

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:49.730
Business used to be declining, but things are better now.

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:55.660
There are new facilities being constructed,
and planetariums for the home are being sold too.

00:16:56.410 --> 00:17:02.580
I think people are attracted to them because there aren't too many places nearby where you can see a sky full of stars.

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:04.670
A small universe.

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:11.880
Yes, although it's just a white hemisphere right now.

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:16.550
But once the projection starts,
it'll turn into a ceiling for the small universe.

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:22.310
In a sense, it's exactly what our ancestors believed the universe was.

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:30.480
The top of the heavens; positioned stars; embedded diamonds; a large heavenly lid.

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:32.110
A mythological world.

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:37.860
Oh my, it's not the time to be explaining things just yet.

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:40.240
You're going to do the navigation?

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:44.370
Yay! I'll be making the final set of explanations in person!

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:46.750
I'll navigate you guys through the summer constellations tonight.

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:50.960
Oh, the red heart, Antares, of the constellation Scorpius.

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:56.300
The wise Cheiron of the Sagittarius hidden amongst the glitter of the Milky Way.

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:59.050
Hey, I'm just about to navigate you through it.

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:01.600
The president's hallucinating.

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:03.770
Oh? I'm a Scorpius.

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:06.770
It was a summer constellation? My birthday's in October.

00:18:07.100 --> 00:18:08.020
I'm a Sagittarius.

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:10.690
Oh, the Scorpius and the Sagittarius.

00:18:10.770 --> 00:18:14.780
Oh, it fits there perfectly!

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:14.650
Hey!

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:15.150
Yes!

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:17.320
Saku-chan.

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:17.860
Hm?

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:20.950
You remembered what you said earlier.

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:22.660
Huh? Oh yeah.

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:25.120
It left a strong impression.

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:30.790
Saku-kun, there are stars you can see in the day and in the rain too.

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:31.880
Do you want to go see them?

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:32.960
What?

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:36.420
It was on a rainy day like today too.

00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:38.800
Playing outside...

00:18:39.220 --> 00:18:40.510
To me, I was being dragged around.

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:42.720
...and inside.

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:44.310
It was lucky for me.

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:46.100
Getting tired of it.

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:48.690
He couldn't bear to watch us, so he took us here.

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:52.650
They don't exist. You liar.

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:54.520
They're fake, aren't they?

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:56.360
Oh? It's true.

00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:59.990
Don't you know what stars visit?

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:03.160
He was a funny man.

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:06.790
I called him a liar. I need to apologize for that.

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:15.500
The dome's ceiling... the universe as humans imagine it.

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:21.090
If you look up, even the stars come to visit.

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:24.720
The planetarium is a small universe.

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:53.560
It's so sad.

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:55.940
It's so sad, Planetarium.

00:20:56.310 --> 00:20:58.150
What's with that sun rise?

00:20:58.570 --> 00:21:01.150
Don't make it bright!

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:04.240
What's with you, Sagittarius! Stand more firm!

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:06.700
Come again.

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:09.200
Bye, Haruko-san.

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:11.200
Good-bye, mademoiselle.

00:21:19.420 --> 00:21:20.880
W-What's with you all of a sudden?

00:21:22.590 --> 00:21:25.800
Oh, come on. I was happy you remembered.

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:26.470
Huh?

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:29.680
You'll catch a cold if you don't use an umbrella.

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:32.890
Oh, look, the umbrellas look like a planetarium.

00:21:32.930 --> 00:21:33.180
Huh?

00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:40.610
That dome is just a plain dome if you look at it from the outside...

00:21:44.240 --> 00:21:45.860
The small universe inside an umbrella.

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:50.030
Above the colorful universes,

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:53.790
beyond the gray clouds...

00:21:56.330 --> 00:21:57.460
summer's approaching.

00:22:02.750 --> 00:22:03.960
It's here!

00:22:04.420 --> 00:22:07.340
Summer equals stars and stars equal all nighters!

00:22:07.630 --> 00:22:10.510
And all nighters equal an overnight camp!

00:22:11.050 --> 00:22:13.100
It's a summer camp!

00:22:22.480 --> 00:22:26.860
I look up at the sky, and I think of you…

00:22:27.150 --> 00:22:30.530
but I can’t find the words,

00:22:31.660 --> 00:22:33.830
I want to tell you,

00:22:33.830 --> 00:22:36.330
but they just slip away…

00:22:36.660 --> 00:22:40.000
almost like Shooting Stars.

00:22:40.500 --> 00:22:44.590
In this Wave of Silence,

00:22:44.960 --> 00:22:48.970
a ray of light flickers the darkness

00:22:49.430 --> 00:22:54.260
playing with my memories

00:22:54.260 --> 00:23:00.100
and releasing my heart.

00:23:00.940 --> 00:23:03.060
Into the future,

00:23:03.060 --> 00:23:11.620
I will have these feelings again!

00:23:12.030 --> 00:23:16.040
No worries, I’m not alone.

00:23:16.290 --> 00:23:21.120
You have taught me I’m not alone.

00:23:21.120 --> 00:23:30.050
Listen to my “Twinkle” story!

00:23:30.180 --> 00:23:34.220
Maybe my voice would reach you.

00:23:35.600 --> 00:23:40.480
I look up at the sky, surrounded by Stardust!

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:49.950
Next time: Until Daybreak

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:49.950
Sora no Manimani

00:23:45.690 --> 00:23:47.110
Next time on Sora no Manimani:

00:23:47.530 --> 00:23:48.230
Until Daybreak.

00:23:48.440 --> 00:23:49.900
The stars are calling us!

00:23:49.950 --> 00:23:54.950
The Astronomy club goes to their first training camp

00:23:49.950 --> 00:23:54.950
at a certain lake-shore.

00:23:54.950 --> 00:23:59.960
Saku experiences for the first time

00:23:54.950 --> 00:23:59.960
what you'd call "a genuine night!?"
